#: ../content/agent/chat/chat.rst:178
msgid "Chat Widget"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/agent/chat/chat.rst:180
msgid "The chat widget is the main component when chatting with other people. It provides a history of all messages in the chat as well as a list of possible actions depending on your permission level."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/agent/chat/chat.rst:182
msgid "The messages can be sent using the text field of a chat in *My Active Chats* widget by either clicking the send icon next to the text field or hitting the Enter key. Shift + Enter can be used to insert a new line into the message."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/agent/chat/chat.rst:184
msgid "Every chat participant has a colored circle icon before his/her name in the chat widget header, which represents the participant availability."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/agent/chat/chat.rst:186
msgid "Green: participant is active (available and online)."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/agent/chat/chat.rst:187
msgid "Yellow: participant is away (available, but there was no request sent to the server from this user for some time set in ``ChatEngine::AgentOnlineThreshold``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/agent/chat/chat.rst:188
msgid "Pink: participant is inactive (chat request is not accepted yet or participant left the chat)."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/agent/chat/chat.rst:189
msgid "Red: participant is unavailable (set via availability button)."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/agent/chat/chat.rst:190
msgid "Black: participant has logged out or session has expired."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/agent/chat/chat.rst:192
msgid "The chat widget has some icons in the top right corner."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/agent/chat/chat.rst:197
msgid "Chat Menu"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/agent/chat/chat.rst:199
msgid "The first triangle icon expands and collapses the chat menu. The menu has several menu items."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/agent/chat/chat.rst:202
#: ../content/agent/tickets/ticket-zoom.rst:464
msgid "Phone ticket"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/agent/chat/chat.rst:202
msgid "Allows you to create a phone ticket to which the current chat will be appended to as an article. After the ticket has successfully created, the chat will get closed automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/agent/chat/chat.rst:205
msgid "Append"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/agent/chat/chat.rst:205
msgid "Allows you to append this chat as an article to a selected ticket. After the article has been created, the chat will get closed automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/agent/chat/chat.rst:208
msgid "Invite"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/agent/chat/chat.rst:208
msgid "Allows you to invite another agent to this chat. You can select from a list of available agents whom you want to invite. Once the agent has invited, a new agent to agent chat request will be sent to this agent. After the request has been accepted, a new internal chat will be established between you and the invited agent. In this internal chat, the invited agent has two more actions available in the advanced actions toolbar: *Observer* and *Participant*."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/agent/chat/chat.rst:211
msgid "Channel change"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/agent/chat/chat.rst:211
msgid "Using this link, you can change the channel for this chat. For the selection of the target channel the same rules apply as for initially selecting a chat channel."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/agent/chat/chat.rst:214
msgid "Download"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/agent/chat/chat.rst:214
msgid "Lets you download the complete history of this chat as PDF."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/agent/chat/chat.rst:217
msgid "New window"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/agent/chat/chat.rst:217
msgid "Opens this chat in a separate popup window. You can use this window in the same way as the chat widget and both the widget and the popup can be used at the same time."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/agent/chat/chat.rst:224
msgid "Observer"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/agent/chat/chat.rst:220
msgid "When you have been invited to a chat by another agent, you can decide if you want to join the chat as observer or participant depending on your permission level. Once you click the action from your toolbar, a new chat widget will be added to the list of your active chats which is the chat you have been invited to."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/agent/chat/chat.rst:222
msgid "If you join the chat as observer, you will only be able to read what others are contributing to the chat and you will be invisible to customer users or public users. Agents will still receive a message that you joined the chat as observer."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/agent/chat/chat.rst:224
msgid "As an observer, you have the possibility to become a participant anytime by using the advanced action toolbar in your chat widget depending on your permission level."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/agent/chat/chat.rst:227
msgid "Participant"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/agent/chat/chat.rst:227
msgid "If you want to contribute something to the chat you have been invited to, you can join it as a participant. Customer users, public users and agents will receive a message that you have entered the chat. As a participant, you can become an observer anytime by using the advanced action toolbar in your chat widget."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/agent/chat/chat.rst:229
msgid "The second circle icon allows the agent to set up a personal monitoring for this chat, which is a three-way switch:"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/agent/chat/chat.rst:231
msgid "Empty circle: no monitoring."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/agent/chat/chat.rst:232
msgid "Empty circle with tick icon: only monitor customer user activity."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/agent/chat/chat.rst:233
msgid "Filled circle with tick icon: monitor all actions."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/agent/chat/chat.rst:235
msgid "When monitoring a chat, browser notifications will show up each time there is a new action in this chat."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/agent/chat/chat.rst:237
msgid "Finally the third close icon makes it possible to close the chat by clicking on the *X*."
msgstr ""

